<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi<br><br> Have you tried to pull the battery, power it off, insert the battery back, power it on with SK2 held down ?<br>That most of the time solve the problem.<br><br>Pulling the reset pin is quite useless, as nothing can survive a battery removal, (when power switch is on) as MCU point of view.<br><br><br>Cheers.<br>---<br>Daniel</div></blockquote>Thanks for your answer.<br>I updated it again but updating CPS and it worked fine. I had previously done it with an old version.<br>Thanks for your answer.<br>greetings<br>73's</div></blockquote>Hello again.<br>On the second day of using it, the same thing happened again. It turns off completely and there is no way to turn it on, not even taking out the battery.<br>If it only happened to me, I assume there is a problem between the firmware and my 1801A. If no one tried it on another 1801A, it's the firmware.<br>Thank you anyway<br>I'll stick with an old version.<br>Greetings<br>LU1EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=3965">LU1EML</a> — Tue May 14, 2024 1:15 pm</p><hr />
